    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) standing as our highest-rated option. While his #8 slot in the order presents a marginal drawback, the confluence of a favorable matchup against Lowder (4.77 xERA) and significant wind assistance makes him an elite play today, provided the 36% rain risk does not lead to a postponement. **Junior Caminero** (71.24) follows closely as a high-floor anchor at third base; his prime position in the #3 hole combined with a favorable lefty-starter matchup against Bennett allows him to thrive even with a slight platoon regression. **Trea Turner** (67.35) remains an essential start, as his dynamic speed profile against Ginn\u2019s slow delivery offers a prime opportunity to secure the stolen bases our roster desperately craves.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (56.46), who was narrowly squeezed out of the high-leverage tier due to a challenging lefty-on-lefty matchup against Quintana. While his park factors and projected SP skill gave him a solid boost, the platoon disadvantage ultimately kept his efficiency below our 60-point threshold for a \"Strong\" start. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Caleb Durbin** (42.95); he remains in our active lineup despite a lower projection because his 100% stolen base upside against Jax is too valuable to leave on the bench, even if his #9 order slot dilutes his run-production potential. We are managing our game caps carefully, keeping stalwarts like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** on the bench due to scheduled off-days or IL designations, ensuring our active slots are reserved for players like **Kyle Schwarber** (61.85), whose consistent xwOBA against Ginn keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" category.",
